[h1]Put the right amount on every shelf[/h1]

Storage Group Quotas lets you set an [b]upper limit for each item[/b] on a shelf, stockpile, or linked shelf group. Linked shelves share one quota, and storable items added by other mods work too.

[h2]Useful around the whole colony[/h2]
[list]
[*]Cap restaurant food shelves at a small serving supply instead of moving the whole freezer into the dining room.
[*]Limit the meals stored in a prison to reduce over-delivery and spoilage.
[*]Limit hay at a barn or feeding area so one high-priority shelf does not pull in the ranch's entire supply.
[*]Arrange ammunition from Combat Extended or other weapon mods into several smaller, ready-to-grab stacks.
[/list]

[b]A quota is a maximum, not a minimum stock target or a new restock order.[/b] Normal RimWorld hauling still decides when items are brought in.

[h2]Choose one of two modes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Entire storage count[/b] — Keep up to X of each selected item across the whole group. Use this when only the total matters.
[*][b]Similar stacks ×N[/b] — Keep up to X in each stack and up to N physical stacks. Total capacity is X × N. Use this for ammunition or supplies several pawns may need at once.
[/list]

With some hauling or reservation mod setups, one physical stack can be claimed by only one pawn or job at a time. Several stacks provide separate pickup targets and can reduce waiting during simultaneous reloads or resupply. For example, [b]25 × 4[/b] allows up to 100 rounds in up to four stacks.

Set a whole category at once, then fine-tune a child category or individual item. Each item type receives its own limit; category values are not one shared mixed-item budget.

[h2]What happens to excess items?[/h2]
Incoming hauling respects the quota. Existing excess is moved by normal hauling to another valid storage area, or to reachable ground outside the group if no storage is available. Similar-stacks mode first tries to rearrange stacks inside the group. Nothing is deleted or teleported.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
Select a shelf or stockpile → click [b]Quotas[/b] → choose a mode → set a category or item value.

[h2]Requirements and compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.6 and 1.7
[*][b]Requires Harmony[/b]
[*]Works with Combat Extended ammunition; Combat Extended is not required
[*]Optional compatibility for Hauler's Dream, Pick Up And Haul, Digital Storage 3.0, and Manipulator Beam Emitter
[*]On RimWorld 1.7, optional integrations also need a compatible 1.7 build of the other mod
[*][b]Incompatible with Stack Gap[/b] — disable it first; old settings are not migrated
[/list]

[url=https://github.com/Steel-Shadow/RimWorld-StorageGroupQuotas]Full documentation, source code, and issue tracker[/url]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]让每个货架都只放刚好够用的数量[/h1]

Storage Group Quotas（存储组配额）可以为物品架、储存区或一组已链接的物品架设置[b]按物品分别计算的存放上限[/b]。链接物品架共享一份配额，其他模组加入的可储存物品也能使用。

[h2]殖民地里的常见用途[/h2]
[list]
[*]限制餐厅食品架只摆少量餐食，避免小人把整座冷库搬进餐厅。
[*]限制囚犯区最多存放多少餐食，减少过量配送和腐坏。
[*]限制牧场或喂食区的干草数量，避免高优先级物品架吸走全部牧草。
[*]把 Combat Extended 或其他武器模组的弹药整理成几堆较小、随时可取的实体堆栈。
[/list]

[b]配额是存放上限，不是最低库存或新的补货命令。[/b]何时入库仍由 RimWorld 的正常搬运决定。

[h2]选择一种模式[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]整个仓库数量[/b] — 整个存储组内，每种选定物品最多保留 X 件。只关心总数时使用。
[*][b]类似堆栈 ×N[/b] — 每堆最多 X 件，最多保留 N 个实体堆栈，总容量为 X × N。适合弹药和其他可能被多个小人同时取用的补给。
[/list]

在部分搬运或预留模组的机制下，一堆实体物品同时可能只能由一个小人或任务占用。多个堆栈能提供彼此独立的取用目标，减少多人同时换弹或补给时的等待。例如 [b]25 × 4[/b] 表示最多 100 发，分布在最多四堆中。

你可以先给整个分类设置数值，再细调子分类或单个物品。每种物品分别使用自己的配额；分类数值不是多种物品共用的一份混合总额。

[h2]超量物品会怎样？[/h2]
新的入库搬运会遵守配额。已有超量物品会通过正常搬运送到其他合法仓储；没有可用仓储时，则放到存储组外可到达的地面。“类似堆栈 ×N”会先尝试在组内整理。物品不会被删除或瞬移。

[h2]使用方法[/h2]
选择物品架或储存区 → 点击[b]存储配额[/b] → 选择模式 → 为分类或单个物品设置数值。

[h2]需求与兼容[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.6 与 1.7
[*][b]需要 Harmony[/b]
[*]可用于 Combat Extended 弹药，但不强制依赖 CE
[*]可选兼容 Hauler's Dream、Pick Up And Haul、【CA】数字存储-Digital Storage 3.0 与 Manipulator Beam Emitter（牵引光束）
[*]在 RimWorld 1.7 中，可选适配还需要对应模组自身提供兼容的 1.7 版本
[*][b]与 Stack Gap 不兼容[/b] — 请先禁用，旧设置不会迁移
[/list]

[url=https://github.com/Steel-Shadow/RimWorld-StorageGroupQuotas]完整说明、源代码与问题反馈[/url]
